@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: why a 595-line function's locals became a struct, and what that bought
' covers: internal/run/spec.go
' covers: internal/run/run.go
' covers: internal/run/**
' covers: cmd/proveo/golden_test.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/main.go (pickProject, scopePage, scopePageAnswer)
' covers: e2e/scope_picker_test.go
'   why there is one backend ... _spec/internal/sbx/sandbox-backend.puml
'
' ── 2026-11-10: ONE GATE DECIDES WHETHER A RUN ASKS FOR A SCOPE ────────────
' resolveWorkspace asked for a monorepo scope whenever stdin was a terminal
' and the wizard was on. It read neither --yes nor PROVEO_SCHEDULE.
'   `proveo run --yes` in a monorepo still opened the picker.
'   [Inference] A scheduled run there opened it too and waited: the scheduler
'   types into a tmux terminal. This rests on reading the gate; no scheduled
'   run was recorded doing it.
' scopeGate(p, tty, wizard, scheduled) now answers one of three:
'   scopeAsk     a headed run that was not told yes: the operator picks
'   scopeRoot    --yes or the scheduler: the repo root, and one line says so
'                  scope: repo root
'                (the Executor, D17: "Repo root, with a line")
'   scopeSilent  --print, no terminal, or the wizard off: the repo root, as
'                before, with no line
' --print stays silent because it starts nothing; the scheduler runs it first
' and reads its output.
' Project discovery runs only when the gate is not silent, so --print still
' pays for none.
' ESC IN THE PICKER CANCELS. fuzzyPickProject returned "" for three things:
' the "<repo root>" row, a finder failure, and Esc. "" means the repo root, so
' Esc started a run on the whole repository. pickedScope now maps the finder's
' ErrAbort to run.ScopeCancelled; chooseScope turns that into
'   cancelled at the scope prompt
' and the run exits 1 before anything is created. A finder failure still falls
' back to the repo root.
' MEASURED on a real terminal (tmux), 2026-11-10: before the change proveo was
' still running 30s after Esc; after it, it printed the line and exited 1.
' WRITTEN TWICE BY CHOICE, AND NOW REPLACED: on 2026-11-11 the tree page took
' fuzzyPickProject's place (the next section). The gate stays; the sentinel
' went.
' Pinned by internal/run/scope_gate_test.go:
'   TestTheScopeGateAsksOnlyAHeadedRunThatWasNotToldYes
'   TestASkippedScopeQuestionTakesTheRepoRootAndSaysSo
'   TestClosingTheScopePickerCancelsTheRun
' by cmd/proveo/main_test.go:
'   TestAClosedScopePageCancelsAndAPageThatCannotDrawKeepsTheRepoRoot
' and by e2e/scope_picker_test.go: TestEscInTheScopePageCancelsTheRun
'
' ── 2026-11-11: THE SCOPE IS PAGE 1, AND THE FORM STEPS BACK TO IT (W-d) ───
' resolveWorkspace did two jobs: it found the repository, and it applied a
' scope to it. The second ran once, before the form, so a scope could not be
' revisited. It is now two functions and a loop.
'   detectWorkspace  once: the GitHub access settings, the repository, the
'                    output directory
'   applyScope       per visit: the mount, the env file, and what that file
'                    sets (evidence, MCP, mise trust)
'   choosePages      the scope page, applyScope, the form; again after each
'                    step back
' The page itself: _spec/internal/choiceui/scope-tree.puml.
' A STEP BACK STARTS OVER FROM A COPY. The form's stage changes Params before
' it draws: the cache seed, the add-on flags, the capabilities. choosePages
' clones Params on entry and restores the clone before each visit, so a
' second visit sees what the first one saw. clone copies every slice and map.
' THE FORM'S ANSWERS SURVIVE THE ROUND TRIP. The form that stepped back goes
' to the next visit, and Form.Adopt copies its answers into every row that
' offers the same options. A locked row, and an option the new scope greys
' out, keep the new form's own answer. The env file depends on the scope, so
' the auth row can differ between two visits.
' THE SCOPE LINE PRINTS ONCE, AFTER THE PAGES. It printed before the form.
' Inside the loop it would repeat on each step back.
' THE PAGES ARE NUMBERED ONLY WHEN BOTH SHOW. A run that asks no scope
' question (--scope, no project found, --yes) draws the form with no page
' and no way back, as before.
' NOT HOISTED: the form's own lookups (dev ports, Android apps, SSH keys)
' run again on each visit. The plan's "a step back re-runs no detection"
' holds for the repository and the project list only.
' THE FORM NAMES WHAT ENTER STARTS (W-j). runOnEnter lists, for the scope the
' visit has: the workspace (a private clone, or the mounted checkout and
' why), "create the sandbox, or re-attach to the one this folder left", and
' "start <target>". The key line counts them.
' THE SANDBOX'S NAME IS NOT ON THE PAGE, though the plan asked for it. The
' name is a hash of the first workspace mount, and the mount plan is built
' after the form, from the form's own answers.
' Pinned by internal/run/pages_test.go: TestTheRunFormNamesWhatEnterStarts
' THE SENTINEL IS GONE. PickProject returns (scope, ok); a closed page is
' ok = false. A page that cannot open the terminal keeps the repo root and
' says so, as a finder failure did.
' Pinned by internal/run/pages_test.go:
'   TestAStepBackReturnsToTheScopePageWhereItWasLeft
'   TestClosingTheScopePageEndsThePagesBeforeTheForm
'   TestARunWithNoScopeQuestionShowsTheFormAloneAndCannotStepBack
'   TestAFormErrorEndsThePages
'   TestACloneSharesNoSliceOrMapWithItsOriginal
' by internal/choiceui/choiceui_test.go:
'   TestAdoptCarriesAnswersToRowsThatOfferTheSameOptions
' and by e2e/scope_picker_test.go:
'   TestTheFormStepsBackToTheScopePageWhereItWasLeft
'
' ── 2026-10-16: ONE BACKEND, ONE INPUT ─────────────────────────────────────
' The docker+egress backend is deleted ("Retire Docker egress"; "Refuse without
' sbx"). MEASURED, run.Do's stages now read:
'   requireSandbox · resolveWorkspace · promptChoices · resolveCredentials ·
'   buildPosture · assembleEnv · launchSandbox
' requireSandbox runs FIRST, before any workspace work, so a host that cannot
' run sbx refuses before a prompt is drawn. Since 2026-10-17 it checks nothing
' else: the PROVEO_SBX off-value stub is gone, Params.Shell went with `--shell`,
' and the "manifest without `docker: sbx`" refusal went with the key (F10:
' requireSandbox(p, d) takes no manifest, run.go:94; a stale key now fails
' manifest loading instead).
' Spec's docker-only fields — SquidConfig, DockerSpec, BrokerFile, the
' inject/ and review/ dirs, the sidecar ModelSpec fields — are gone from
' spec.go; dockeregress.Input is gone with its package. selectBackend and
' execute collapsed into launchSandbox.
' cmd/proveo/run_golden_test.go is DELETED: its three cases were docker
' plans. MEASURED: no test now pins a whole `--print` run.Do byte for byte;
' TestSandboxPlanGolden calls sandbox.Spec directly. The resolve-path hole
' described below is therefore OPEN again (repo-simplification.puml T1
' proposed re-recording it as sbx goldens).
'
' ── 2026-10-17: RUN STATE IS A RUN DIR, NOT AN EGRESS DIR (N13, DONE (wt)) ──
' MEASURED: Spec.EgDir is Spec.RunDir (spec.go:21, "per-run state: the sbx
' kit, policy log and staged clone env"), filled by RunDirOf(sid) =
' <StateDir>/runs/<sid>; sandbox.Input.EgDir is Input.RunDir; the egDir
' parameters of runlog.Artifacts, CapturePolicyLog and CaptureMemoryEvidence
' are runDir. RunRoots() now returns only <StateDir>/runs. The retired egress/
' root was swept for one release, then removed. Test: TestRunStateLivesUnderRuns
' (env_names_test.go). The picker's "egress" row (sbx's policy baseline) is
' a different concept and keeps its name.
' 2026-10-18 (N25): Do moved RunDirOf after runlog.Open and ui.TeeTo so the
' deprecated state-root warning reached the transcript. The alias and its
' warning were removed after v0.2.0; the ordering remains.
'
' ── THE PROBLEM WAS THE STACK FRAME ────────────────────────────────────────
' doRun held SIXTY top-level locals. That is not a size complaint: it means the
' function's contract was invisible. Nothing could be moved out of it without
' first proving, by reading all 595 lines, which later line still needed the
' value — and every one of moves 2 to 5 paid that cost again.
'
' Spec is those locals, named. It sits ABOVE the backend input: sandbox.Input
' is built FROM it at the seam. HISTORY: while two backends existed it was
' deliberately not a merge of sandbox.Input and dockeregress.Input, so no
' docker-only field (PidsLimit, ReviewSocket) was legible to sbx.
'
' ── THE ORDER OF THE TWO STEPS IS THE WHOLE TRICK ──────────────────────────
' Enumerating Spec came FIRST, as a change that altered nothing else: the struct
' was declared, filled where each local settled, and the consumers switched to
' read it. Only then was the body sliced. Slicing first would have meant
' discovering the contract and changing the structure in one diff, with no step
' where a green suite meant anything.
'
' ── WHERE THIS DEPARTS FROM THE PLAN, AND WHY ──────────────────────────────
' The plan names seven stages:
'   resolveWorkspace · resolveCredentials · promptChoices · buildPosture ·
'   selectBackend · execute · teardown
' The shipped set differs in two ways, both forced by output ORDER:
'   * promptChoices runs BEFORE resolveCredentials, not after. The prompt needs
'     the env-file lookup, and the auth report needs the answers, so the real
'     order is workspace -> lookup -> prompt -> auth.
'   * assembleEnv is a stage of its own. The plan folds it into
'     resolveCredentials, but posture is rendered BETWEEN the two; moving either
'     across that line changes the order the operator reads them in.
'   * teardown is not a stage. It is `defer` inside execute, so a signal
'     mid-run unwinds exactly the way a normal exit does.
' Stages are contiguous slices of the original statement order. Nothing was
' reordered, because reordering is precisely what the golden below forbids.
'
' ── THE PROOF HAD A HOLE, AND IT WAS THIS MOVE'S HOLE ───────────────────────
' Moves 2 to 5 were proved by the plan goldens. Those call dockeregress.Assemble
' and sandbox.Spec DIRECTLY: they pin the backends and say nothing about the
' resolve path that feeds them — which is the only thing this move touches. The
' resolve path's sole coverage was the e2e ladder, which is slow and skips
' without credentials.
' cmd/proveo/run_golden_test.go closed that hole: it drove a whole `--print` run
' under a pinned environment and pinned the bytes, ui narrative included. It was
' written and captured BEFORE the split, so its passing afterwards was evidence
' rather than decoration. It was deleted 2026-10-16 with the docker plans it
' rendered; the rules below are how a replacement must be written.
'
' ── A GOLDEN OVER THE RESOLVE PATH IS A GOLDEN OVER THE OPERATOR'S SHELL ────
' The resolve path READS the environment, so anything it can see and the test
' does not pin becomes a property of whoever ran it. Measured: a developer with
' ARCHITECT_MODEL exported got three `-e ..._MODEL=` flags, a DARK_MODE flag, an
' `------ egress ------` section and three keyless-role warnings the recorded
' golden had never seen — a diff that says nothing about the resolve path and
' everything about whose shell ran the test. So EVERY credential the path can
' see is pinned empty (otherwise the operator's own keys decide which providers
' are "detected"), and so is everything else it reads. PROVEO_DIND was pinned
' off for the same reason while it warned when set; since 2026-10-17 it is
' unread, so a replacement golden need not pin it.
'
' Two things are pinned ON rather than off, and the distinction is the point:
'   the gh mount   a real line of the plan, so pinning it OFF would DROP
'                  coverage. It is pointed at a directory the test creates —
'                  always present, always at a path the scrubber can rewrite.
'                  Unpinned it stat-ed the developer's own ~/.config/gh, so the
'                  line existed only for developers who use gh.
'   the agent uid  `--user 501:20` is a fact about the macOS laptop that recorded
'                  the golden and `--user 1000:1000` a fact about every Linux CI
'                  runner. There is NO env override to pin, and there should not
'                  be: a test-only switch on the uid the agent runs as is
'                  production surface bought for a test's convenience. It is a
'                  display property, so it SCRUBS, like the session id.
'
' ui.Default caches os.Stderr at init, so swapping the files is not enough to
' capture output; the anonymous wrapper hides *os.File, which is what makes ui
' render plain text instead of colour escapes.
title internal/run — the contract that was a stack frame

participant "cmd/proveo\nwiring" as CMD <<app>>
participant "run.Do" as DO <<app>>
participant "Spec\nthe resolved contract" as SPEC <<data>>
participant "sandbox.Input" as SBX <<cloud>>

CMD ARROW_MAIN DO : Params (flags) + Deps (terminal, gh, docker)
DO ARROW_ERROR DO : requireSandbox — refuse unless sbx is ready
DO ARROW_MAIN SPEC : detectWorkspace · choosePages · resolveCredentials
DO ARROW_MAIN SPEC : buildPosture · assembleEnv
SPEC ARROW_QUEUE SBX : launchSandbox

note over CMD
  **Deps keeps this package honest.** Prompts,
  the gh session and image pulls stay in
  cmd/proveo and arrive as functions.
end note

note over SPEC
  **One gate for the scope question.** ""--yes""
  and the scheduler take the repo root and
  print ""scope: repo root"". Esc on the page
  cancels the run; it no longer means root.
end note

note over DO
  **Refusal comes first.** ""requireSandbox""
  runs before any workspace work, so a host
  that cannot run sbx stops before a prompt.
end note

note over SPEC
  **Sixty locals, named once.** The values the
  plan called doRun's hidden contract: sid,
  egDir (now RunDir), uid/gid, mounts, workdir,
  lookup, detected, homePlan.
end note

note over DO
  **The output dir is created host-side, before
  either backend sees it.** ""docker run -v""
  invents a missing path as ROOT, and sbx does
  not invent it — it asks 'create it?
  (y/N)', which no unattended run can answer.
end note

note over DO
  **Converted with gofmt -r, not regex.** A text
  pass had already rewritten a string LITERAL.
  An AST rewrite cannot reach into strings or
  comments — which is why that damage was
  caught rather than shipped.
end note
@enduml
